💡 **SUGGESTION: `j.step` fallback can never match — run-jobs objects have no `step` property** _(carried over from the first round: the rework fixed everything else here, this line is untouched)_

```js
var names = (jobs.jobs || []).map(function (j) {
    return j && (j.name || j.step); // job name == check context
});
```

`GET /actions/runs/{id}/jobs` job objects carry `name` (and a nested `steps` **array**), never a scalar `step` — so `j.step` is always `undefined` and the fallback is dead. If the intent was matrix/step-level robustness it does nothing; if not, drop it (`j && j.name` suffices). Harmless today, but a reader will assume the fallback does something.

