{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: once-per-head marker is posted even when the rerun set covers only part of the cancelled contexts** _(re-posted: unaddressed at head 7b495d75)_

`rcTargets` can legitimately cover a **subset** of `rcCancelled`: contexts whose cancelled runs are already attempt-2+ (skipped by design), or whose job names don't match any walked run (`jobs?per_page=50` cap, job-name/context drift). The marker is then posted anyway, and from the next tick on the `rcReported` check short-circuits **before** the mapping probe — the head is "remedied" forever while the uncovered contexts still read `CANCELLED` (the exact gh-682 BLOCKED symptom), and even the per-tick `"no rerunnable ... skip"` warn disappears into the marker.

```js
if (rcReported) {
    console.log('  ⏭️  ' + key + ' cancelled checks already re-run for head — waiting on the rerun');
    continue;
}
```

Fix: post the marker only when `rcTargets` covers **all** of `rcCancelled` (or list the uncovered contexts in the marker text), so an unmapped context keeps visibly retrying/warning instead of being silently latched shut by a partial remediation. Test to add: two cancelled contexts where only one maps to an attempt-1 run → no marker on that tick.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}

{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: copy-paste bug in the new test helper — `it[k] = extra` drops the `[k]` index** _(re-posted: unaddressed at head 7b495d75)_

```js
function prItem682(n, extra) {
    var it = { key: 'pr-' + n, labels: ['ai_validating'], issueNumber: null,
               prNumber: n, draft: false, branch: 'ai/gh-1202',
               pr: { headSha: '898efd4' } };
    if (extra) { for (var k in extra) { if (extra.hasOwnProperty(k)) it[k] = extra; } }
    return it;
}
```

Every sibling helper in this file does `it[k] = extra[k]` (lines 855, 1682, 1864, 2041) — this copy assigns the whole `extra` object to every key. It is latent today only because every call site is `prItem682(1202)`; the first caller that passes `extra` (e.g. `prItem682(1202, { labels: ['ai_validated'] })`) gets `{ labels: {labels: [...]}, prNumber: {labels: [...]}, ... }` and a silently wrong fixture — which also blocks the `ai_validated`-latch test case the suite will need for the stale-run fix. One-character fix.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment3.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `number:` vs `pullRequestId:` — keep one spelling per tool in this file** _(re-posted: unaddressed at head 7b495d75)_

This new call site passes `number: ticket.prNumber` to `github_get_pr_comments`, while the other 3 call sites in this file (1584→1587, 1828→1831, 3013→3015) use `pullRequestId:`. Both aliases work against the current dmtools runtime (verified live), but if the tool ever tightens its input schema, every site should already agree — `pullRequestId` is the canonical name per `js/common/trackers.js` ("the number argument keeps the tool's canonical pullRequestId name"). Same payload, just match the file's existing contract. (`github_create_comment` sites in this file do use `number:` — only the `github_get_pr_comments` spelling needs aligning.)
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment4.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `rcRunIds` is dead code** _(re-posted: unaddressed at head 7b495d75)_

```js
var rcRunIds = [];
var rcSeen = {};
rcTargets.forEach(function (t) {
    if (rcSeen[t.runId]) return;
    rcSeen[t.runId] = true;
    rcRunIds.push(t.runId);
